      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T01:03:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No. The \u0027if\u0027 conditions were intentional. See the bug in the comment. (+danalbert for visibility \u0026 he wanted the behavior.)\n\n#apex symbols are implemented by a library that is included in an APEX (i.e. NotInPlatform() \u003d\u003d true). #systemapi symbols are those from outside of an APEX",
      "parentUuid": "44baddea_0c05eacf",
      "revId": "5c890d743cf01a65cb56372ed78b8a2c9f032fb7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2eef3bc5_c7b04691",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1878380
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T03:16:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For this specific error in b/265485106, should the annotations for `libmediandk`\u0027s map.txt be updated from `#apex` to `#systemapi`? I looked at installed-files.txt from go/ab and this library is installed in /system/lib\n\nAs a more general question, shouldnt these annotations be a no-op in the build system anyways for this API surface? A library cannot be both included in an APEX _and_ included in the platform. Hacky CS query: https://cs.android.com/search?q\u003dsystemapi%20apex%20f:%5C.txt%20case:yes\n\nThe stubs generated by passing `--apex` to the libraries originating from apexes and `--systemapi` to the libraries originating from platform will be equivalent if we passed `--apex --systemapi` to both these categories.",
      "parentUuid": "a933c789_23f8f807",
      "revId": "5c890d743cf01a65cb56372ed78b8a2c9f032fb7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7821fe10_c67f249d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T09:51:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e should the annotations for libmediandk\u0027s map.txt be updated from #apex to #systemapi? \n\nYes. I didn\u0027t notice that the APIs were marked as #apex. Since they are part of the non-updatable platform, they should be #systemapi.\n\n\u003e A library cannot be both included in an APEX and included in the platform\n\nCorrect. But the two different annotations were created for reviewing purpose and for preventing accidental promotion (or demotion) of API between #systemapi and #apex. See b/191371676.\n\n\u003e The stubs generated by passing --apex to the libraries originating from apexes and --systemapi to the libraries originating from platform will be equivalent if we passed --apex --systemapi to both these categories.\n\nRight. But as I said above, such a change wouldn\u0027t prevent a user from mistakenly adding \"#apex\" symbols to a platform-provided library or \"#systemapi\" symbols to an APEX-provided library. That\u0027s what Dan (in general his team) wanted to prohibit.",
      "parentUuid": "2eef3bc5_c7b04691",
      "revId": "5c890d743cf01a65cb56372ed78b8a2c9f032fb7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
