      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T18:57:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003eYes. I didn\u0027t notice that the APIs were marked as #apex. Since they are part of the non-updatable platform, they should be #systemapi.\n\nAck. I think `libmediandk` and `libandroid` are the only two platform libraries that contain # apex. I have created aosp/2393584 and aosp/2395614 to update this. This should also fix the libmediatranscoder error in `riscv`.\n\n\u003e Correct. But the two different annotations were created for reviewing purpose and for preventing accidental promotion (or demotion) of API between #systemapi and #apex. See b/191371676.\n\nThanks Jiyong, this makes sense to me now. I have converted this CL to a \"documentation change only\" CL. b/191371676 contains some very useful context which I think we should to the documentation.\n\n\nSomething I would like to discuss with you and Dan is how these should map to Multi-tree. My previous understanding was that both of these two symbols contribute to the same API surface, but upon multiple reads of b/191371676, I think my understanding was incorrect. I will follow up on this conversation with you and Dan offline.",
